{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1085544-void-engineers-what-are-aliens","id":1085544,"title":"Void Engineers-What are Aliens?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-29T13:02:02-07:00","id":1085544,"title":"Void Engineers-What are Aliens?","content":"I know alien can describe a multitude of beings in the WoD but my current interest is in the deep umbral space past horizon. Can anyone give me details on established beings or how to generate such things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T13:57:59-07:00","id":1085574,"title":"","content":"Take spirits, give them an alien description","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T14:21:17-07:00","id":1085583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1085544-void-engineers-what-are-aliens?p=1085574#post1085574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take spirits, give them an alien description</div> </div> </div> </div>I have seen how werewolf treats it's two Aliens and so far I have treated alien things like spirits unless they are special and more physical. Those I so far have stated with fomori rules.<br /> <br /> I was told that the Grey's and something from the edge of reality lurked in the world of mage. Was hoping to hear more about these, and even more beings that are part of Canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T14:35:44-07:00","id":1085590,"title":"","content":"I think stats for Greys are in the old VE book, maybe the players guide to the technocracy? All else fails grab the bygone bestiary and have fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T08:12:24-07:00","id":1086205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freederp92</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1085544-void-engineers-what-are-aliens?p=1085583#post1085583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have seen how werewolf treats it's two Aliens</div> </div> </div> </div>That entry that introduces the Inquisitors and Vhujunka pretty much explicitly notes that they aren't extraterrestrial aliens, which seems to be the subject of the thread, but rather wild cards and mysterious unknowns. Also, Werewolf is really, really different when it comes to dividing how the cosmos works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T10:22:43-07:00","id":1086247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freederp92</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1085544-void-engineers-what-are-aliens?p=1085583#post1085583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have seen how werewolf treats it's two Aliens and so far I have treated alien things like spirits unless they are special and more physical. Those I so far have stated with fomori rules.<br /> <br /> I was told that the Grey's and something from the edge of reality lurked in the world of mage. Was hoping to hear more about these, and even more beings that are part of Canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as rules for what &quot;aliens&quot; should like as a pile of numbers, seems like you're doing what there is to do. Aliens, aka EDE's, are spirits and, if you're out in the Deep Umbra, they don't need to manifest, use Reach, Possess or anything. You're on their turf. (Which means all aliens sorta melt and teleport when you blast them....) <br /> <br /> For the sake of convenience, you could just stat them out in a more physical way out using the rules for the appropriate Charm.<br /> <br /> Seems like fomori rules might work too. It's re-jiggering them for a different purpose, but if you want your EDE's to be like aliens from science fiction movies, books, etc. it's probably a decent way to have them not do the fundamental things that Werewolf-based spirits do that is just so NOT like what such aliens do. <br /> <br /> I think when I ran a &quot;SoE in Space&quot; game, I just statted out aliens when I needed to do so and didn't worry about what the game said they were. Little blood-thirsty vegetable people from the steaming jungles of Venus were set up just like an animal, human, mage or vampire, not like a spirit, so they could use their blasters on them, do damage, kill them and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T16:55:17-07:00","id":1086384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freederp92</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1085544-void-engineers-what-are-aliens#post1085544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know alien can describe a multitude of beings in the WoD but my current interest is in the deep umbral space past horizon. Can anyone give me details on established beings or how to generate such things?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an end of the world for mages focused on aliens in ToJ: Ascencion, it's focused on the grays and on a race of 4th dimensional beings with a name impossible to remember. It's a must read if you're interested in the topic. There's a few more creatures labeled as &quot;alien horrors&quot; in the Book of Worlds: The Watchers of the Deep, and another race of difficult name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}